WEBVTT

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.280
It's almost time.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.110
I'm so nervous.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.820
My little flower, believe in yourself.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.950
And believe in us too, senpai.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.200
If we work together,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.790
we can even make miracles happen.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.590
We'll always protect you.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.750
You gave us something precious.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.340
This time, we'll give something to you.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.350
It's all right. I'm sure you can do it.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.270
<i>On a stage that's sure to 
glitter more than a dream</i>

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.600
<i>Together we'll play</i>

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.150
<i>Dreamin' Starlight Dreamin' Night</i>

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:55.150
<i>SHINY RAY</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.290
<i>A melody that crosses the 
night sky connecting the stars</i>

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.580
<i>Even my emotions overflow from my body</i>

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.920
<i>Let's climb a rainbow high in the sky</i>

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:21.260
<i>Like a colorful palette it brings us smiles</i>

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:33.190
<i>The rising sun makes sleeping 
buds bloom beautifully</i>

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:38.570
<i>On a stage that's sure to 
glitter more than a dream</i>

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.910
<i>Together we'll play</i>

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.040
<i>Dreamin' Sunrise Dreamin' Sunrise</i>

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.290
<i>I'll squeeze your hand and never let go</i>

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.670
<i>Our fortunes quietly overlap</i>

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.360
<i>Dreamin' Sunrise Dreamin' Day</i>

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.880
<i>SHINY RAY</i>

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.140
Magic-Kyun! Renaissance.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.980
<b>Magic-Kyun! Renaissance</b>

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.990
#1 Brilliantly Blooming Renaissance

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.360
Mom, your sparkles...

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.780
...are so pretty.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.910
Like magic!

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.570
Thank you, Kohana.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:11.170
When I grow up, I'm going to shine too.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:13.920
I'm sure you will.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.170
<i>You can do it, Kohana.</i>

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.310
It's okay. I'm sure I can do it.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.460
<i>The Hoshinomori School of Magical Arts.</i>

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.220
<i>Mom, I was able to transfer to your alma mater.</i>

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.820
<i>I'm going to study here and 
become just like my mom.</i>

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.950
<i>I know I can do it!</i>

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.480
All of you were admitted to the 
Hoshinomori School of Magic

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.640
because of your talent for the magical arts.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.830
Da Vinci, Mozart, Murasaki Shikibu, Michelangelo,

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:25.470
Shakespeare, Bach, Picasso, Gaudi.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.540
I hope you'll study hard 
every day so you can approach

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.540
the level of these pioneers 
of the magical arts.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.660
<i>An artista.</i>

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.460
<i>I'll work hard. I'll work as hard as I can!</i>

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.880
<i>Such beautiful sparkles.</i>

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.050
<i>They're sort of warm.</i>

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.740
<i>They're like threads of light.</i>

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.610
Not bad, newbie.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:04.700
Thanks, senpai.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.740
Amazing.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.200
So he's the Monochrome Prince 
I've heard so much about.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.520
His paintings are wonderful.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.190
Isn't he a new student?

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.460
He's incredible for a younger boy.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.460
<i>The Monochrome Prince?</i>

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.660
<i>Oh, his outfit is monochrome.</i>

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.460
<i>And so is his painting!</i>

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:27.380
His paintings are monochrome, 
but he sparkles with all kinds of colors.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.400
<i>How strange.</i>

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.160
Your artistic sense is impressive.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.870
It's no big deal.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:36.720
<i>"Squeak?"</i>

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.560
<i>Wow, how dynamic.</i>

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:45.780
<i>I wonder what it is.</i>

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.110
<i>Maybe a wild boar?</i>

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.740
<i>These sparkles smell sweet, like vanilla.</i>

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.370
Senpai, that's an impressive tiger.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.920
What? It's a cheetah.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.610
Can't you tell by looking at it?

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.250
What? No.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.080
<i>There's no way anyone could tell,</i>

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.040
What?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.670
<i>but he sparkles nonetheless.</i>

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.820
<i>He must be an incredible artista.</i>

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.370
Jeez, Angelo.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.200
You're always joking around.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:17.890
Angelo?

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.310
Just kidding.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.640
I'm always serious.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.410
Bang.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:36.160
Angelo!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.790
Were those wings sparkles?

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.170
His dancing was amazing.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.510
It's Suminomiya.

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:45.630
He's doing it again.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.170
What? He's going to write on that?

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.280
Suminomiya-kun's art is beautiful enough.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.930
But when it comes to calligraphy, 
he's indiscriminate.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.660
It's beautiful.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.820
I wouldn't expect less from Suminomiya.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.960
This isn't right either.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.040
He's out of energy.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.820
Again?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.100
<i>It's a little pointy.</i>

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.370
It's beautiful.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.410
There are sparkles all over the place here.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:30.040
I can't believe I'm actually 
a student at Hoshigei.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.560
It's like a dream.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.890
I'm glad I didn't give up.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.310
They're like diamonds.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:36.000
But what is this?

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.920
They feel a little cold.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:16.910
E-Excuse me...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.210
You're heavy.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.540
S-Sorry.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.350
Thank you for saving me.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.440
You're a second-year.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.010
I'm also a purple student...

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.800
I'm a transfer student.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.440
I was on my way to the dorms.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.060
Nice to meet you.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:51.120
I'm sorry for talking so much.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.690
But they were so beautiful.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.460
Your sparkles were so beautiful.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.030
That's none of your business.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.620
What? Oh...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.140
I-I'm sorry.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.270
Um, thank you.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.820
Wrong way.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.040
What? Oh, is it this way?

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:19.400
Hey.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:19.930
Yes?

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.920
The dorm isn't that way.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.620
Hurry up.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.270
Thank you so much.

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:40.810
I appreciate the help.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.910
Well, well.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.080
You don't waste any time, do you?

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.240
You had the king walk you here.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:50.920
The king?

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:52.970
Ichijoji Teika.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.170
A prodigy who's practically 
a king around here.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:58.140
He's a prodigy. I see.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.240
His singing was wonderful.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.010
Yeah.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.760
They say he can sing any song 
immediately after hearing it.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.520
He probably doesn't even need to practice.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.730
Th-That's incredible.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.830
You're the transfer student, right?

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.800
I'm your roommate, Chikamatsu Juri.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.900
Nice to meet you.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.260
Nice to meet you.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.610
I'm Aigasaki Kohana.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.860
What? Aigasaki?

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:22.610
What?

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.460
How wonderful.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.580
I'm surprised.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:35.500
I can't believe my roommate 
is Aigasaki Sakura's daughter.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:38.310
You know my mom?

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.730
Everyone knows her.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.380
She was a world renowned artista

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.180
and an alumnus of this school.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.390
She passed away, right?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.390
Yeah, when I was little.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:57.650
I came to this school because 
I wanted to be like my mom.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:59.340
I see.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:05.610
Then, why didn't you come to 
Hoshigei in the first place?

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.160
Well, actually...

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:10.990
I had a bad fever the day 
of the entrance exam.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.870
I couldn't take it.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.040
Yikes.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.840
But even after attending a regular 
school, I couldn't give up.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.880
I see. So you took the transfer exam.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.640
Yeah. That's right, Juri-san.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.480
"That's right, Juri."

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:26.360
What? Oh.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.140
That's right, Juri.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:29.140
Yeah.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.270
I'll call you Kohana, too.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.340
Okay.

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.630
Anyway, you're amazing, Kohana.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.300
What?

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:40.280
Apparently, they offer the 
transfer exam every year.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.680
But I've never heard of anyone passing it.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.080
R-Really?

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.660
Well, I'm not surprised after hearing 
you're Aigasaki Sakura's daughter.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.640
Kohana, do you do flower arranging, too?

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.680
Yeah.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:51.740
Give it a try.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.660
I want to see what kind of light you shed.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:55.600
What?

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.060
Come on, hurry up.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:59.210
I-I can't do that.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.550
I haven't taken any lessons yet.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.520
There you go again.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.310
Really, I can't.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.430
Go on, go on.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.090
Um...

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:07.820
Huh?

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:15.080
What? Seriously?

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:19.000
Most Hoshigei students can at 
least manage some magical arts

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.360
by the time they start.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.730
Some students even go pro 
while they're still students.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:24.360
What?

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.500
We're second-years,

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.910
so most students are already at the 
level that they can use magical arts.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.430
Uh-oh....

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:35.420
For you.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.900
Magic-Kyun!

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.230
Magic-Kyun!

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.010
Renaissance.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.480
I had no idea.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:50.510
Some people can produce sparkles even 
if they haven't been taught how.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.360
Okay. I should be able to 
practice in secret here.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.750
I should give it a shot.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.070
Until now, I assumed I couldn't produce them.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:07.360
But if I think I can, I might be able to.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.700
No, I'm sure I can.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.200
They're not coming.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:16.710
They're still not coming!

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.760
It's no use.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.800
Maybe I can't do it after all.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.050
My friends were so supportive, too.

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:33.670
Congratulations, Kohana.

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:34.970
Your dream came true.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:38.340
It's incredible that you got into Hoshigei.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:42.060
Kohana, you never gave up 
on flower arranging.

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:46.860
Promise you'll show us when 
you learn to do magical arts.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:48.660
You can do it, Kohana.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:54.290
I think I'm already letting them down.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.080
The king's sparkles.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.590
They're so beautiful.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:45.500
How beautiful.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.530
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.760
Your sparkles were so beautiful, 
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.160
You again?

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.890
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:03.560
Um, you practice too?

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.440
No, I was just singing.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:18.990
This staircase is unusual.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.640
You can't go up there.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:24.360
What?

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.380
They're the Scala Artista.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.130
The Scala...?

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:31.590
I see. You don't know yet.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:36.560
Every year, the Prince and Princess 
chosen to be the Best Artista

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:38.140
climb these steps.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:40.770
Best Artista?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:43.060
Prince? Princess?

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:47.110
They're the male and female students 
recognized as the most exceptional of that year.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.590
Every student at Hoshigei wants to be chosen.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.280
I want to be one, too.

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.520
You're awfully confident.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:00.290
What kind of magical art do you use?

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.810
I can't.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.280
Maybe I was naïve.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:15.480
I worked really hard because I was 
desperate to get into Hoshigei.

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:18.800
But I'm having to face some harsh truths.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:21.860
Even though I've worked so hard,

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.390
I'm wondering if it was all for nothing.

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:24.980
Hard work?

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:26.480
What?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:31.280
The moment you doubt your hard work
 is the moment it becomes worthless.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:35.490
Only those who continue to believe 
are able to achieve results.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:41.240
Your hard work will never betray you.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:44.090
Your hard work will never...

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.410
You're right.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.130
This is no time to be feeling down on myself.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:52.500
As long as I work hard, I can do it.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:59.410
Don't tell anyone we met here.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.140
Huh?

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:02.890
What? Um...

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.020
Wait!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.270
What do you want?

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:13.730
Thank you.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.990
I'll work hard. I'll do my best!

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:26.750
What?

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.140
The sparkles...

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.840
These are my first sparkles.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:54.840
This is the first time I've made any.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:57.150
Yeah, you did it.

00:18:58.660 --> 00:18:59.900
Yeah!

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.410
See you later.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.660
Thank you, King.

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:08.080
It's Ichijoji Teika.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.080
Sure, Ichijoji-kun.

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.590
All right. I'll do my best!

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:25.600
We have a transfer student.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:26.480
Seriously?

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:27.580
A transfer student?

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.690
I've never seen one before.

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.100
How unusual.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.100
What's her major?

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.500
Quiet.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:39.470
You can sit...

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.430
Oh, perfect.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.990
Go sit next to Chikamatsu.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:43.760
Okay.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:44.500
That's all.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:46.420
Ah, o-okay.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:49.150
Teacher, tell us more about her.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.300
Shut up. I'm busy.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:52.500
You never do anything right.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.290
Yeah, yeah. You guys figure 
something out on your own.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:56.990
You always say that.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.750
I value independence in my students.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.120
Good to see you.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.380
He didn't even tell them my name.

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:05.650
Todo-sensei's always like that.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.390
I can hardly believe how unmotivated he is.

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:12.300
Regarding this year's 
Hoshinomori Summer Festival...

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.640
Summer Festival?

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:18.270
It's the school's summer cultural festival.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:18.900
Really?

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:22.860
These three will be your second-year 
executive committee members.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.240
Let's see...

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:26.700
Ichijoji Teika.

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.100
Yes.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.920
I'm not surprised Ichijoji-kun was chosen.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.210
Suminomiya Aoi.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:35.600
Suminomiya isn't here today, either.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.390
Suminomiya doesn't come to class.

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:40.900
He wanders around by 
himself doing calligraphy.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:43.720
Was he the guy writing on the school walls?

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:47.220
Ichijoji, tell Suminomiya later.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.220
Yes, sir.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:52.980
And the third student is...

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:55.950
Aigasaki Kohana.

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:57.900
What? I was chosen already?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.420
What? Did he say Aigasaki?

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:01.920
What? That Aigasaki?

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:03.130
The transfer student?

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.120
Seriously?

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:04.890
What?

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.280
Um, I...

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.350
So you're Aigasaki's daughter.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:18.000
What?

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:20.750
You're my enemy.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.510
Is the transfer student really an Aigasaki?

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.810
What? She's Aigasaki Sakura's daughter?

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.760
This isn't good.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:27.470
Um, excuse me...

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:53.160
<b>Magic-Kyun! Renaissance</b>

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:12.740
<i>Teika, I heard Aigasaki's daughter 
transferred to the school.</i>

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:14.610
<i>You know what you have to do.</i>

00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:20.960
<i>You must become the Artista Prince.</i>

00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:24.480
Yes, brother.

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:29.770
I thought I didn't need anything else.

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.630
Not until I met you.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:35.560
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.350
"I Can Only See You."

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:39.960
Magic-kyun for you.
